so much of our early understanding of  the characters  worlds and relationships of mass effect  is defined by  one conflict or another the rachni war  the geth war the krogan rebellions the  genophage so it only makes sense that  our understanding of how  humans fit into milky way society is  also defined by conflict  to the turians and most other aliens  it's called the relay 314 incident  but humans refer to it as the first  contact war  but let's back up a bit in 2148 35 years  prior to the events of mass effect 1  humanity discovers evidence of an  ancient sentient alien species called  the protheans on mars  if you want a bit more context on who  and what the protheans were  you can watch our previous mass effect  lore video anyway this discovery  accelerates humanity's technological  advancements when it comes to space  travel  the ruins also mention an interstellar  highway composed of technology called  mass  relays which allows near instantaneous  interstellar travel  and apparently one of those mass relays  is in the solar system  a year later humanity discovers that  what was previously believed to be one  of pluto's moons  is in fact the mass relay mentioned in  the prothean ruins with a bit of work  humanity reactivates the relay allowing  them to travel to the arcturus system  where they find even more relays  thinking nothing of it humanity starts  reactivating every relay they can  find traveling far and wide across the  milky way galaxy  eight years later in 2157 humanity  reactivates mass relay 314.  as it turns out the turians witnessed  the deed and opened fire because  activating dormant relays is  highly illegal in citadel space why is  it illegal  well that's a very long story and a  whole other video but basically  activation of a previously dormant relay  over 2000 years prior  led to the discovery of the raknai which  led to the rachni war which led to the  uplifting of the krogan  which led to the krogan rebellions which  led to the genophage which is why the  turian salarians and krogan  all have rather tense relationships with  each other there's  so much more to those stories but that's  the basic gist of why the citadel  outlawed reactivation of dormant relays  it could potentially  lead to the discovery of a dangerous  species now  turians are nothing if not sticklers for  the rules which is why they opened fire  and what they perceive to be someone  breaking the law  small problem humanity has no idea that  what we are doing  is wrong we have never encountered a  living sentient species before  no one had told us the rules so what  could have been an easily explained  misunderstanding  instead erupted into all-out conflict  that humanity would come to call  the first contact war humanity's  response to being attacked is to get  recon on the threat  and humans being humans we don't just  send scouting probes into terrain space  to spy on our enemy  we send in scouting probes armed with  nuclear fusion  warheads you know just in case a probe  is discovered and needs to be destroyed  to avoid the turians learning more about  us  thankfully no probes are discovered  unfortunately  those warheads are still floating around  in turian space by the time of the  events of mass effect 1  a dirty little secret that humanity  hopes the rest of the galaxy never  discovers  though humanity claims a few victories  in the war the turians take the  advantage early on pushing humanity back  to sean xi  the human colony established just  outside mass relay 314  the turians then simply set siege to the  colony bombarding it with orbital  strikes  though the leader of the colony's  garrison general williams puts up a  strong effort  he ultimately surrenders making him the  first human leader  to ever surrender to an alien threat  williams would be demoted and face  prejudice from military command for the  rest of his very short career  as a result and the stigma against him  would pass on to his son  who also enlisted william's  granddaughter ashley williams would  inherit this family curse next  breeding her blunt it's me against  everyone else attitude  and initial discomfort at working  closely with aliens like tali liara  garris and rex  it's not racism not really members of  their species will always be more  important to them than humans are  but enough of that believing they have  won the turians relax  only to be surprised by the appearance  of humanity's second fleet  at this point the citadel council  notices that a fairly  major conflict is brewing under their  noses and chooses to step  in negotiating peace talks between  humans and turians  and ending the three-month war humanity  finally learns that the milky way is  inhabited by many different species  most of whom coexist peacefully under  the leadership of the citadel council  after seeing that humanity has a knack  for waging war  the council views humans as a much  needed asset and ally  and invites them into the galaxy-wide  alliance humanity accepts  it isn't a smooth transition though  after hearing about how humanity's first  contact with an  alien race went down most species begin  to view all humans as bullies prone to  violence this perception is not helped  by humanity's aggressive push to have  footholds across the galaxy  and a dominant voice in the citadel  humans face extreme prejudice from other  species for  years especially from turians like saren  who had lost loved ones to the war  pro-human groups begin popping up in  response most notable  is terra firma a human political party  which opposed humanity's integration  into milky way society  and cerberus a human paramilitary group  that works to improve humanity's  standing  in the face of alien prejudice to ease  the tension the council orders the  tyrians to pay reparations to humanity  eventually the two species become trade  partners further improving relations  between them  to symbolize the friendlier relationship  between their two governments  despite the continued strain between  veterans of the war humans and turians  decide to work together  putting their combined military might  and engineering architecture into one  starship that ship would become the ssv  normandy a symbol of what can be  achieved when mankind works together  with aliens  instead of trying to kill them and its  first mission is the opening chapter  of mass effect 1 and that's the history  behind story of and ramifications of the  first contact war a war that  in the grand scheme of things is still a  relatively recent conflict in the milky  way's history by the start of the mass  effect trilogy  hopefully you're now a little bit more  prepared to jump into mass effect  legendary edition  knowing why some humans on the ssv  normandy aren't immediately comfortable  serving alongside aliens despite what  the ship represents but speaking of  first contact which mass effect alien  species left the biggest first  impression on you  like you saw them for the first time and  just immediately wanted to know  everything about them personally i think  the quarians are fascinating and i loved  unearthing their history throughout the  trilogy and talking to tally  usually flirtatiously leave your answers  in the comments below and subscribe to  the channel for more mass effect lore  videos like this one  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

